# Code

- Use Tailwind CSS for all styling.
- Use `--color-primary-*`, `--color-secondary-*`, `--color-base-*`, ... custom classes over tailwind's default classes.
- Extract reusable UI sections into components.
- Reuse components whenever possible.
- Only use React when necessary (interactive islands). So only <10% of the time.
- Keep files small and focused. One component per file.
- Write concise commit messages.
- Use the Icon component from astro-icon/components for icons and the material design icons collection (mdi:)

## Project structure

### 🔧 **Core Files & Folders**

- **`src/`** *(required)*: Your site's source code

  - `pages/` *(required)*: Routes of your site (e.g. `index.astro` → `/`), can also be Markdown/MDX

  - `components/`: Reusable UI components (Astro, React, etc.)

  - `layouts/`: Page templates using `<slot />` (e.g. `BaseLayout.astro`)

  - `styles/`: CSS/Sass files (e.g. `global.css`)

  - `content/` or other subfolders: Markdown/MDX content (e.g. blog posts)

  - `assets/`: Images to be processed/optimized by Astro and other  

- **`public/`**: Static files served as-is (e.g. `favicon.svg`, `robots.txt`)

  - ⚠️ Files here are **not optimized or bundled**
